Z||000001||mrfixit58||09-08-2000||03:47 PM||||Are you planning on fixing it up a little at a time or plunking down another $1000 right away to get it on the street? Can you find anything better for $1200 - $1500 in your area? I'm alway a little leary about trying to put something on the street that has accident damage. For $200, it may make a better parts car. <P>My $0.02 worth,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
